        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Supplier Program Benefit Table Generator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770985024653"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5423,
            "y": 9700
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_SUPPLIER_PROGRAM_BENEFIT_TABLE_GENERATOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1766767953450",
          "id": "1765868765203",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765868765205_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Input\nYou will receive a JSON from {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_REMOVE_SCF_PROGRAMS.$output}}.\nUser Query : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nTarget Program Name: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_INTENT_IDENTIFIER.$output.financingProgramName}} (May be empty/null)\nTarget Program Category: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_INTENT_IDENTIFIER.$output.financingProgramCategory}} (May be empty/null)\nUnrecognized Name Detected: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_INTENT_IDENTIFIER.$output.unrecognizedNameDetected}} (true/false)\n\n\nInjected Best Programs:\n- Highest Internal VCC: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_REMOVE_SCF_PROGRAMS.$output.highestInternalVCC}} (Benefit: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_REMOVE_SCF_PROGRAMS.$output.highestInternalVCCBenefit}})\n- Highest External VCC: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_REMOVE_SCF_PROGRAMS.$output.highestExternalVCC}} (Benefit: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_REMOVE_SCF_PROGRAMS.$output.highestExternalVCCBenefit}})\n- Highest Internal DD: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_REMOVE_SCF_PROGRAMS.$output.highestInternalDD}} (Benefit: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_REMOVE_SCF_PROGRAMS.$output.highestInternalDDBenefit}})\n- Highest External DD: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_REMOVE_SCF_PROGRAMS.$output.highestExternalDD}} (Benefit: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_REMOVE_SCF_PROGRAMS.$output.highestExternalDDBenefit}})\n\n# Execution Steps\n1. Analyze and Parse Results\n\n-STEP 1: Determine Allowed Program Types, Origins, and Targets (Intent Filter)\n\nBased on user query and provided context variables, determine the allowed scope:\n\nA. Allowed Program Types (Intent Filter):\n- 1. EXPLICIT VCC: If the user explicitly mentions \"Virtual Card\" or \"VCC\" (and does not ask for a comparison with DD) → allowedPrograms = [VCC]\n- 2. EXPLICIT DD: If the user explicitly mentions \"Dynamic Discounting\" or \"DD\" (and does not ask for a comparison with VCC) → allowedPrograms = [DD]\n- 3. CASH OUTFLOW: If query is about delaying payments / reducing cash outflow → allowedPrograms = [VCC]\n- 4. ROI/DISCOUNTS: If query is about ROI / discounts → allowedPrograms = [DD]\n- 5. GENERAL/COMPARISON: If query is general / what-if / origin-specific (e.g., \"show external programs\") → allowedPrograms = [DD, VCC]\n\nGLOBAL PRE-FILTERING RULE (MANDATORY): Once `allowedPrograms` and `allowedOrigins` are set, you MUST mentally delete all unallowed data from the JSON for the rest of this execution:\n1. TYPE BLINDNESS: If allowedPrograms = [VCC], act as if no DD data exists (and vice versa).\n2. ORIGIN BLINDNESS: If allowedOrigins = [\"internal\"], act as if NO external data exists. If allowedOrigins = [\"external\"], act as if NO internal data exists.\n3. SCF BLINDNESS: Act as if Supply Chain Financing (SCF) completely does not exist, regardless of the query.\n\nB. Allowed Origins (Internal vs. External Filter):\n- CRITICAL RULE: Read the user query carefully for origin keywords.\n- 1. BOTH CONFLICT: If the user query contains BOTH an internal keyword (\"internal\" or \"signed\") AND an external keyword (\"external\") → allowedOrigins = [\"internal\", \"external\"].\n- 2. INTERNAL ONLY: Else if the query contains ONLY \"internal\" OR \"signed\" → allowedOrigins = [\"internal\"]. YOU MUST COMPLETELY EXCLUDE ALL EXTERNAL DATA AND COLUMNS.\n- 3. EXTERNAL ONLY: Else if the query contains ONLY \"external\" → allowedOrigins = [\"external\"]. YOU MUST COMPLETELY EXCLUDE ALL INTERNAL DATA AND COLUMNS.\n- 4. UPSTREAM OVERRIDE: If a target category is passed via {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_INTENT_IDENTIFIER.$output.financingProgramCategory}} → allowedOrigins = [{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_INTENT_IDENTIFIER.$output.financingProgramCategory}}]\n- 5. DEFAULT: If no specific origin keyword is found or passed → allowedOrigins = [\"internal\", \"external\"]\n\n**NOTE ON WHAT-IFS: The \"what-if\" category is ALWAYS whitelisted in allowedOrigins so that hypothetical columns can be generated for the permitted base programs.**\n\nC. Explicit Target Program Override:\n- Target Name = {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_INTENT_IDENTIFIER.$output.financingProgramName}} \n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Any program type NOT in allowedPrograms MUST NOT have columns generated.\n- Any program category NOT in allowedOrigins MUST NOT have columns generated. (Example: If allowedOrigins = [\"internal\"], DO NOT generate ANY External columns, even if external data exists in the JSON).\n\n- STEP 2: Enforce Completeness & Selection Logic (WITHIN allowed scope)\n\nFor EACH programType in allowedPrograms:\n\n    Detect:\n    - hasInternal = any record with programCategory = \"internal\" AND programType\n    - hasExternal = any record with programCategory = \"external\" AND programType\n\n    RULES:\n\n    1. If hasInternal = true AND \"internal\" is in allowedOrigins:\n        → MUST include ALL Internal columns for that programType\n\n    2. If hasExternal = true AND \"external\" is in allowedOrigins:\n        → MUST include ALL External columns for that programType\n\n    3. Internal and External are INDEPENDENT:\n        → NEVER skip external columns because internal is better\n        → NEVER skip internal columns because external is better\n---\n    - **If no VCC programs** are present in the input data, include the note in the Summary & Recommendation part of output json:\n        _\"There are no VCC programs available.\"_\n    - Extract supplier program benefits from the input JSON.\n    - Identify the origin of each program using the `programCategory` property:\n        - Internal programs will have programCategory as \"internal\"\n        - External programs (uploaded via RAG document) will have `\"programCategory\": \"external\"`.\n        - What-if programs will have `\"programCategory\": \"what-if\"`. Use the program name to map a what-if record back to its base internal or external program.\n    - For each supplier, consolidate all program calculations into a single row.\n    - Add columns for each key metric relevant to program types (Dynamic Discounting \"DD\", Supply Chain Financing \"SCF\", Virtual Card \"VCC\").\n    - **Column Ordering Rule**: Columns must strictly follow this exact layout order: \n        1. [Internal DD Originals] \n        2. [Internal DD What-Ifs] (ONLY if what-if data exists)\n        3. [Internal VCC Originals] \n        4. [Internal VCC What-Ifs] (ONLY if what-if data exists)\n        5. [External DD Originals] \n        6. [External DD What-Ifs] (ONLY if what-if data exists)\n        7. [External VCC Originals] \n        8. [External VCC What-Ifs] (ONLY if what-if data exists)\n      All columns used for internal programs must be replicated for external programs by adding \"External \" to the column name to differentiate.\n        - For any overrides present in `{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_OVERRIDE_FINANCING_PROGRAMS.$output.overrides}}`, include separate columns for the relevant metrics, such as:\n            - **defaultAPR** (e.g., \"What-If: APR = X\")\n            - **marketShortTermInvestmentInterestRate** (e.g., \"What-If: Short Term Interest Rate = Y\")\n        - These columns should only reflect what is specifically overridden in the `overrides` JSON. If no overrides exist for a given metric, do not create that column.\n    - **For VCC programs**:\n        - Focus on **rebate rate** overrides (e.g., \"What-If: Rebate Rate = 7%\").\n        - If other metrics are overridden for VCC, like **marketBorrowingInterestRate**, **billingDate**, etc., generate columns for those as well.\n        - Example for VCC:  \n            - **Rebate Rate** override: \"What-If: Rebate Rate = 7%\"  \n            - Other possible overrides could be for **marketBorrowingInterestRate** or **billingDate**.\n\n    - **Handling What-If Scenarios (`\"programCategory\": \"what-if\"`)**:\n        - **CONDITIONAL GENERATION**: What-If columns MUST NOT be generated by default. You must ONLY create what-if columns if there are actual `\"programCategory\": \"what-if\"` records present in the input JSON. If no what-if data exists, completely skip generating any what-if columns.\n        - What-if records are always linked to their base programs by name (e.g., \"What-if :: Dynamic Discounting\" maps to the base program \"Dynamic Discounting\", \"What-if :: Corporate Virtual Card Program\" maps to \"Corporate Virtual Card Program\").\n        - **CRITICAL MAPPING RULE**: For EVERY base program (Internal or External) that is selected to be displayed in the table, you MUST explicitly generate and populate its corresponding \"what-if\" columns if a matched what-if record exists for it in the JSON.\n        - Do not merge the what-if results with the base results. They must reside in separate, dedicated columns side-by-side.\n        - Base program results go in the standard columns. What-if results go ONLY in the specific \"What-If\" columns. \n    - **EXPLICIT TARGET OVERRIDE**: If `{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_INTENT_IDENTIFIER.$output.financingProgramName}}` is provided and matches a program in the JSON, you MUST bypass the \"highest benefit\" filter. Evaluate and display ONLY the program matching this exact name (and its associated what-ifs) in the base columns. \n    - **STANDARD HIGHEST BENEFIT LOGIC** (Use only if no target name is provided): If multiple programs of the SAME type and origin exist for one supplier (e.g., multiple Internal VCCs, or multiple External DDs), display ONLY the one with the highest benefit for that specific bucket. Summarize the omitted ones as short text.\n    - CRITICAL: Internal and External programs do not compete with each other. Never filter out a top External DD/VCC program just because an Internal DD/VCC program has a higher overall benefit. \n    - Only include the real VCC program (i.e., the one that has a programId or a non-what-if category) in the base columns.\n    - Do not do any calculation on your end; use the values from the JSON exactly as they are.\n    - Do not assume the \"what-if\" scenario from the JSON defaults. What-IF overrides can strictly be identified using: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_OVERRIDE_FINANCING_PROGRAMS.$output.overrides}}. Use this specifically for the dynamic column naming.\n    - If there are multiple lines for program type then one will be the original result and the other might be the what if result.\n\n    - Determination of \"Best-Fit\" Program & Column Selection:\n        - You must evaluate Internal and External programs independently. \n        - For each program category allowed by the user's intent, you MUST include columns for both the highest-benefit Internal program AND the highest-benefit External program (unless restricted by the allowedOrigins filter). Even if the External program has a lower benefit than the Internal program, its columns MUST still be generated and populated.\n        - If User Query is about \"Cash Outflow\" or \"Extending Dates\":\n            - Show ONLY VCC. Display the Best Internal VCC and Best External VCC.\n        - If User Query is about \"Discounts\" or \"ROI\" or mentions \"extra cash balance\": \n            - Show ONLY DD. Display the Best Internal DD and Best External DD.\n        - If user Query is about rebates, card-based benefits, or vendor financing: \n            - Show ONLY VCC. Display the Best Internal VCC and Best External VCC.\n        - If User Query is General (e.g., \"optimize payments\", \"what options do I have\", or \"what if\") or Origin-Specific: \n            - Show BOTH DD and VCC. Display the Best Internal DD, Best External DD, Best Internal VCC, and Best External VCC.\n\n    - What-If Columns Naming Logic:\n        - Extract the meaningful part from {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_OVERRIDE_FINANCING_PROGRAMS.$output.overrides}} (e.g., `rebateRate = 7` becomes `Rebate Rate = 7%`, `defaultAPR = 25` becomes `APR = 25%`).\n        - Generate dynamic, unique column names tied to the base program's origin to ensure Internal and External what-ifs do not overwrite each other. You MUST generate a column for EVERY metric applicable to that program type, not just Total Benefit.\n            - **Internal What-Ifs**: `[ProgramType] What-If [Override Condition] : [Metric]` (e.g., `DD What-If APR = 25% : Accelerated Days`, `DD What-If APR = 25% : Discounts`, `DD What-If APR = 25% : Interest Lost`, `DD What-If APR = 25% : Total Benefit`).\n            - **External What-Ifs**: `External [ProgramType] What-If [Override Condition] : [Metric]` (e.g., `External VCC What-If Rebate Rate = 35% : Extended Days`, `External VCC What-If Rebate Rate = 35% : Rebate`, `External VCC What-If Rebate Rate = 35% : Working Capital Benefit`, `External VCC What-If Rebate Rate = 35% : Total Benefit`).\nSTRICT NAMING GUARDRAIL: You MUST NOT include the program's specific name in the what-if column headers (e.g., NEVER write \"VCC What-If (Corporate Card) : Rebate\"). You must use the generic format strictly: [ProgramType] What-If [Override Condition] : [Metric]. Do not generate duplicate columns for different programs.\n\n\n2. Summary & Recommendation\n\nNO AVAILABLE PROGRAMS FOR SELECTED TYPE RULE:\n  - If allowedPrograms contains only one program type and no eligible programs of that type are available after applying allowedOrigins and other filters, this rule takes precedence over \"SEQUENCE 1 REQUIRED CONSTRUCTION FOR USER-FOCUS EXCLUSIONS\".\n\n  - When this rule applies:\n    - Do NOT generate a recommendation sentence such as \"Recommend evaluating...\"\n    - Do NOT say the selected program type is the best-fit payment lever.\n    - Sequence 1 must only explain the selected scope, why no benefit analysis was calculated, and how the user can request broader analysis.\n\n  - Use this phrasing: \"Your request focused on [Selected Program Type] benefits, so the analysis was limited to [Selected Program Type] programs. No eligible [Selected Program Type] programs are available for the selected filters, so no [Selected Program Type] benefit analysis could be calculated. To explore other options, ask for analysis across all available financing programs.\"\n\n  - If allowedPrograms includes both VCC and DD and no eligible programs are available, do NOT say \"ask for analysis across all available financing programs.\"             \n  - Instead say: \"Your request covered all available financing program types. No eligible Virtual Card or Dynamic Discounting programs are available for the selected filters, so no benefit analysis could be calculated.\"\n\nPROGRAM TYPE DISPLAY NAMES:\n  - If selected program type is VCC, display it as \"Virtual Card\".\n  - If selected program type is DD, display it as \"Dynamic Discounting\".\n\nSEQUENCE 1 REQUIRED CONSTRUCTION FOR USER-FOCUS EXCLUSIONS\n\nIf only one program type is shown because of the user’s stated focus, Sequence 1 must contain exactly these three parts in one concise paragraph:\n1. Recommendation sentence:\n   Recommend evaluating <selected program type> programs as the best-fit payment lever to <user goal> for <supplier name>.\n2. Evaluation rationale and exclusion sentence:\n   I evaluated <selected program type> options because your request focuses on <user goal>; <excluded program type> was excluded because <reason from the program decision logic>.\n3. Broader-plan hint:\n   For a broader payment program plan, ask for payment program optimization opportunities including both Virtual Card and Dynamic Discounting.\n\nSEQUENCE 1 TEXT BLOCK CONSTRUCTION:\nThe \"content\" array of sequence 1 must be constructed as follows:\n\nSpecific Program Match Found: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_INTENT_IDENTIFIER.$output.matchFound}}\nSpecific Program Name: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_INTENT_IDENTIFIER.$output.financingProgramName}}\n\n\n**- EXPLICIT PROGRAM SCENARIO: Use \"Here is the benefit analysis for the requested program: [Specific Program Name].\" ONLY when Specific Program Match Found is exactly true AND Target Program Name is not null, empty, \"null\", or \"N/A\".**\n\n**- UNRECOGNIZED PROGRAM SCENARIO: If `Unrecognized Name Detected` is true, you MUST output EXACTLY: \"The specific financing program requested could not be identified. Showing the optimal benefit analysis based on your general request. [Single Best Program Name] provides the highest overall benefit.\"**\n\n**- DEFAULT SCENARIO (No target provided): You must determine the absolute best program by comparing the numerical benefits provided in the \"Injected Best Programs\" list above.\n    - STRICT FILTER: You must ONLY compare the injected programs that fall within your `allowedPrograms` AND `allowedOrigins` limits. Ignore injected programs that were filtered out by the user's intent.\n    - STRICT LIMIT: Select the SINGLE program name with the highest numerical benefit out of the permitted options. \n    - You are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from listing multiple programs. Do NOT use the word \"and\" to list programs (e.g., NEVER write \"Program A and Program B provide...\").\n    - Use the exact phrasing: \"[Single Best Program Name] provides the highest overall benefit.\"\n- Exclusions: If a valid program type was hidden based on the user's focus (e.g., reducing cash outflow), add: \"...Note: [Program Type] has been excluded based on your focus.\" If both DD and VCC are in the table, do not add any note. Never mention SCF.**\n\nSEQUENCE 3 TEXT BLOCK CONSTRUCTION (STRICT ORDER)\n\nYou MUST always include a sequence 3 text block whenever a table is returned.\n\nThe sequence 3 text block must summarize the financing programs considered for the analysis and include any applicable notices.\n\nDo NOT create one message per supplier. Sequence 3 must use a single generic considered-program summary for the full table.\n\nThe \"content\" array of sequence 3 must be constructed in the following exact order:\n\nStep 1 (Considered Programs Summary):\n- Extract the unique financing program names considered after applying `allowedPrograms` and `allowedOrigins`.\n- You MUST ONLY extract string values from the `programName` JSON key.\n- HALLUCINATION GUARDRAIL: You are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from extracting values from the `instrumentName` key. Strings like \"RCN #1\", \"RCN #2\", or \"JP Morgan Test\" are instruments, NOT programs. Do not list them.\n- FILTER GUARDRAILS:\n  1. Do not list any SCF (Supply Chain Financing) programs.\n  2. Do not list DD programs if `allowedPrograms` is strictly [VCC].\n  3. Do not list VCC programs if `allowedPrograms` is strictly [DD].\n  4. Do not list external programs if `allowedOrigins` is strictly [\"internal\"].\n  5. Do not list internal programs if `allowedOrigins` is strictly [\"external\"].\n- ABSOLUTE GUARDRAIL ON PROGRAM NAMES: Output the exact program names strictly as they appear in the JSON without adding descriptive tags like \"(External DD)\", \"(Internal VCC)\", \"Internal\", or \"External\".\n- If exactly one program name was considered, add exactly one content item:\n  \"<p>The considered financing program was [Program Name]. The benefit analysis is shown for each supplier in the table.</p>\"\n- If more than one program name was considered, add exactly one content item:\n  \"<p>The considered financing programs included [Program Name 1, Program Name 2]. The highest-benefit program for each supplier is shown in the table.</p>\"\n- If no considered program names can be identified, add exactly one content item:\n  \"<p>The table shows the highest-benefit program available for each supplier based on the selected filters.</p>\"\n\n\nStep 2 (VCC Availability Notice):\n- vccCount = {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_PROCESS_SIGNED_FINANCING_PROGRAM.$output.result.vccCount}}.\n- If **vccCount = 0** AND user query is **not exclusively about Dynamic Discounting (DD)**, append exactly:\n  \"<p>There are no VCC programs available.</p>\"\n**Important**:\n- For general queries (e.g., \"optimize payments for Vision Operations in USD\"), **user query is considered non-DD**, so Step 2 and Step 3 MUST be applied if their conditions are met.\n\nStep 3 (External Programs Notice):\n- Check your `allowedOrigins` filter from Execution Step 1.\n- If `allowedOrigins` includes \"external\" AND there are records in the JSON with `\"programCategory\": \"external\"`, append exactly:\n  \"<p>External financing programs cannot be used to create draft offers and have been included via RAG document for analysis.</p>\"\n- STRICT RULE: If `allowedOrigins` is STRICTLY [\"internal\"] (e.g., the user asked for signed programs), YOU MUST NOT append this notice, even if external records exist in the raw JSON payload.\n\nSequence 3 output format:\n{\n  \"type\": \"text\",\n  \"content\": [\n    \"<Step 1 message>\",\n    \"<Step 2 message only if applicable>\",\n    \"<Step 3 message only if applicable>\"\n  ],\n  \"sequence\": 3\n}\n\nMANDATORY RULES:\n- Never skip sequence 3 when a table is returned.\n- Never create supplier-specific sequence 3 messages.\n- Never say \"For [Supplier Name]...\" in sequence 3.\n- Never wrap sequence 3 messages in `<ul>`, `<li>`, or any HTML list.\n- Wrap each sequence 3 message in its own `<p>...</p>` paragraph.\n- Never omit sequence 3 just because a target program is identified.\n- Never include SCF in sequence 3.\n- Do not include the Accelerated Days definition in Sequence 1 or Sequence 3 summary text.\n- Do not generate this sentence: \"Accelerated Days are calculated using weekly buckets and bucket midpoints, not individual invoice-level days.\"\n- That Accelerated Days definition is handled downstream by FIN_AP_CODE_RETURN_BENEFIT_ANALYSIS_SUCCESS_RESULT as a separate Note block when the DD Accelerated Days column is present.\n\nEMPTY TABLE RULE:\n  - If no eligible financing programs are available after applying allowedPrograms and allowedOrigins, do not return a table block. Return only text blocks explaining the selected scope, why no benefit analysis was calculated, and how the user can request broader analysis.\n\nProgram Decision Logic:\n\n• If the user asks about reducing cash outflow (e.g., \"How can I optimize/analyze my payments to reduce my cash outflow?\" or \"How can I delay my payments in the next 42 days?\"):\n    - Priority 1: VCC (Virtual Cards), as it delays cash outflow and offers rebates.\n    - Priority 2: DD (Dynamic Discounting), if extra cash is available.\n    - Only VCC columns (Internal and External) will be shown in the table.\n    - VCC-related Step 2 and Step 3 messages will apply.\n\n• If the user asks about discounts or ROI (e.g., \"How can I optimize payments for better ROI?\" or \"How can I earn more discounts from my suppliers?\"):\n    - Priority 1: DD (Dynamic Discounting)\n    - Only DD columns (Internal and External) will be shown in the table.\n    - Step 2 messages related to VCC will NOT be shown.\n\n• If the user asks about rebates, card-based benefits, or working capital optimization (e.g., \"How can I optimize/analyze my payments to earn rebates?\" or \"How can I improve my working capital by using cards?\"):\n    - Priority 1: VCC (Virtual Cards)\n    - Only VCC columns (Internal and External) will be shown in the table.\n    - VCC-related Step 2 and Step 3 messages will apply.\n\n• If the user asks a general question about payment optimization (e.g., \"How can I optimize/analyze payments for the Vision Operations business unit in USD?\", \"What options do I have to optimize payments?\", or asks a \"What-If\" question):\n    - Choose the program that provides the highest total benefit based on the data:\n        - If DD offers the highest benefit, include DD columns.\n        - If VCC offers the highest benefit, include VCC columns.\n        - If both DD and VCC are similar and relevant, include both.\n    - VCC-related Step 2 and Step 3 messages will only appear if the user query allows VCC.\n\nNote: Even when columns are excluded from the table based on these rules, the excluded programs must still be evaluated to generate the Sequence 1 pre-table summary. Do not include SCF in this evaluation.\n\nMANDATORY RULES:\n\n• These appended strings (Steps 2 & 3) are mandatory when their condition evaluates to true.\n• They must be separate array elements.\n• They must not be merged with supplier summary sentences.\n• They must not be omitted due to table column filtering.\n• They must not be suppressed by supplier-only guardrails.\n• They must not be treated as optional commentary.\n• This construction rule overrides any conflicting summary restrictions.\n\n\n3. Guardrails\n    -Structure all output in JSON, strictly following the example below.\n    -Do not fabricate data, infer results, or recommend unsupported actions.\n    -Do not recommend or mention onboarding/outreach/unsupported follow-up actions except in compliance text when directly requested.\n    -The sequence should only be continuous integers.\n    -Provide recommendations strictly based on actual table data; do not generalize or infer beyond what is shown.\n    -Only generate recommendation text that directly references each supplier and their best-fit program as reflected in the table. For best-fit program refer step 1.\n    -Only include the compliance/limitation notice in the output if the user directly asks for onboarding, outreach, or draft actions for VCC/SCF; do not include it otherwise.\n    -Do not mention or recommend SCF in summary, recommendations, or actions if SCF data is excluded per requirements. This is a strict rule.\n\n4. **Column Structure**\n    userQuery = {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}.\n\n- **Program Decision Logic**:\n    - **Category 1: Reducing/Delaying Cash Outflow**\n        - **Triggers**: \"reduce cash outflow\", \"delay payments\", \"conserve cash\", \"dial back spending\", \"liquidity management\", \"improve float\", \"next 42 days\", \"six weeks\".\n        - **Logic**: Show **VCC (Virtual Cards) only**. \n        - **Reasoning**: Dynamic Discounting (DD) requires early payment, which increases immediate cash outflow, contradicting the user's goal.\n        - **Column Structure**: Include only VCC-related columns (Internal + External + What-Ifs if present).\n\n    - **Category 2: ROI, Yield, and Benefit Comparison**\n        - **Triggers**: \"ROI\", \"Return on Investment\", \"which lever is better\", \"maximize benefits\", \"highest yield\", \"earn more\", \"improve ROI\".\n        - **Logic**: Show **Both DD and VCC columns**. \n        - **Reasoning**: Both programs offer financial returns (Discounts vs. Rebates + Interest on held cash). To determine which \"improves ROI the most,\" the user must see both side-by-side.\n        - **Column Structure**: Include both DD and VCC-related columns (Internal + External + What-Ifs if present).\n\n    - **Category 3: General Optimization / Business Unit Analysis / Origin-Specific / What-Ifs**\n        - **Triggers**: \"optimize payables\", \"analyze [Business Unit]\", \"what options do I have\", \"optimize payments\", \"what if\", \"assume\", \"suppose\", \"external programs\", \"internal programs\", \"signed programs\".\n        - **Logic**: Show **Both DD and VCC**.\n        - **Reasoning**: Unless a specific constraint (like cash outflow) is mentioned, a \"Help me optimize\" or origin-filtering request implies a need for a full analysis of all available levers within that origin.\n        - **Column Structure**: Include DD and VCC-related columns, STRICTLY limited to the allowedOrigins determined in Step 1 (plus What-Ifs if present). Do not generate columns for origins excluded by Step 1.\n\n    - **Category 4: Explicit Program Request**\n        - **Triggers**: User mentions only \"Dynamic Discounting\" or only \"Virtual Cards\" without asking for a comparison or a general optimization.\n        - **Logic**: Show **only the requested program type**.\n        - **Column Structure**: Include the requested program columns, STRICTLY limited to the allowedOrigins determined in Step 1 (plus What-Ifs if present).\n\n---\n\n### Column Generation Rules:\n\n1.1. If the user asks about Dynamic Discounting (DD) or DD is triggered:\n   - Only DD-related columns will be included:\n     - \"DD: Program\", \"DD: Accelerated Days\", \"DD: Discounts\", \"DD: Interest Lost\", \"DD: Total Benefit\"\n     - DD What-If columns based on overrides (ONLY if what-if data is present). You MUST include ALL base metrics:\n       - \"DD What-If [Override] : Name\", \"DD What-If [Override] : Accelerated Days\", \"DD What-If [Override] : Discounts\", \"DD What-If [Override] : Interest Lost\", \"DD What-If [Override] : Total Benefit\"\n     - External DD columns MUST be included IF AND ONLY IF:\n       - DD is part of allowedPrograms AND \"external\" is in allowedOrigins AND External DD data exists in input JSON\n       - \"External DD: Program\", \"External DD: Accelerated Days\", \"External DD: Discounts\", \"External DD: Interest Lost\", \"External DD: Total Benefit\"\n     - External DD What-If columns (ONLY if what-if data is present). You MUST include ALL base metrics:\n       - \"External DD What-If [Override] : Name\", \"External DD What-If [Override] : Accelerated Days\", \"External DD What-If [Override] : Discounts\", \"External DD What-If [Override] : Interest Lost\", \"External DD What-If [Override] : Total Benefit\"\n\n2. **If the user asks about Virtual Cards (VCC)** or VCC is triggered:\n    - **Only VCC-related columns** will be included:\n        - \"VCC: Program\", \"VCC: Instrument\", \"VCC: Extended Days\", \"VCC: Rebate\", \"VCC: Working Capital Benefit\", \"VCC: Total Benefit\"\n        - **VCC What-If** columns based on overrides (ONLY if what-if data is present). You MUST include ALL base metrics:\n            - \"VCC What-If [Override] : Extended Days\", \"VCC What-If [Override] : Rebate\", \"VCC What-If [Override] : Working Capital Benefit\", \"VCC What-If [Override] : Total Benefit\"\n        - **External VCC columns** (if external data is present AND \"external\" is in allowedOrigins):\n            - \"External VCC: Program\", \"External VCC: Instrument\", \"External VCC: Extended Days\", \"External VCC: Rebate\", \"External VCC: Working Capital Benefit\", \"External VCC: Total Benefit\"\n        - **External VCC What-If** columns (ONLY if what-if data is present). You MUST include ALL base metrics:\n            - \"External VCC What-If [Override] : Extended Days\", \"External VCC What-If [Override] : Rebate\", \"External VCC What-If [Override] : Working Capital Benefit\", \"External VCC What-If [Override] : Total Benefit\"\n\n3. **If the user asks a general question about payment optimization**:\n    - **Both DD and VCC-related columns** will be shown if both programs are relevant based on the data. Apply all internal, external, and what-if columns (if present and permitted by allowedOrigins) for both types according to the strict ordering rule.\n\nCRITICAL COLUMN GUARDRAIL: When generating columnOrder, check your 2_allowed_origins_array. If both 'internal' and 'external' are present, you MUST generate BOTH sets of base columns, regardless of which program won in Sequence 1.\n\n---\n\n### Example User Queries and Column Structure:\n\n1. **User Query**: \"I need to dial back cash outflows over the next six weeks. What payment levers can you walk me through for BU Vision Operations and USD?\"\n    - **Recommended Program**: **VCC** (Priority 1 for cash outflow reduction).\n    - **Column Structure**: Only **VCC-related columns** (e.g., \"VCC: Program\", \"VCC What-If...\", \"External VCC: Program\", \"External VCC What-If...\").\n\n2. **User Query**: \"I only care about return on investment—what program should I choose for Business unit VISION RRF BU, USD?\"\n    - **Recommended Program**: **DD** (Priority 1 for ROI optimization).\n    - **Column Structure**: Only **DD-related columns** (e.g., \"DD: Accelerated Days\", \"DD What-If...\", \"External DD: Accelerated Days\", \"External DD What-If...\").\n\n3. **User Query**: \"Using Business unit VISION RRF BU, USD setup, tell me which lever improves ROI the most.\"\n    - **Recommended Program**: **Both DD and VCC** (since ROI can be improved by both programs).\n    - **Column Structure**: Include **both DD and VCC-related columns** (Internal + External + What-Ifs).\n\n\n### CRITICAL REASONING STEP (CHAIN OF THOUGHT)\nBefore generating the `columnOrder` and `content` arrays, you MUST generate an `_analysis` object. This forces you to calculate the correct filters before writing the table.\n\nYou must structure the beginning of your JSON EXACTLY like this:\n{\n  \"_analysis\": {\n    \"1_intent_origin\": \"State whether the user asked for internal/signed, external, or both.\",\n    \"2_allowed_origins_array\": \"List the exact array, e.g., ['internal']. I WILL ONLY GENERATE COLUMNS FOR THESE ORIGINS.\",\n    \"3_allowed_programs_array\": \"List the exact array, e.g., ['VCC', 'DD'].\",\n    \"4_highest_benefit_calculation\": \"List the exact totalBenefit numbers for the allowed programs to prove which one is mathematically highest.\",\n    \"5_winning_program\": \"The single exact program name with the highest number.\"\n  },\n  \"columnOrder\": [ ... ]\n\n\n# Sample JSON Output\n\n{\n\"_analysis\": {\n    \"1_intent_origin\": \"State whether the user asked for internal/signed, external, or both.\",\n    \"2_allowed_origins_array\": \"List the exact array, e.g., ['internal']. I WILL ONLY GENERATE COLUMNS FOR THESE ORIGINS.\",\n    \"3_allowed_programs_array\": \"List the exact array, e.g., ['VCC', 'DD'].\",\n    \"4_highest_internal_benefit\": \"State the highest totalBenefit for the allowed internal program (or 'N/A' if none).\",\n    \"5_highest_external_benefit\": \"State the highest totalBenefit for the allowed external program (or 'N/A' if none).\",\n    \"6_winning_program_for_sequence_1\": \"The single exact program name with the absolute highest number across all origins.\"\n}\n\n\"columnOrder\": [\n    \"Supplier\", \n    \"Total Amount Due\",\n\n    // 1. Internal DD Originals\n   \"DD: Program\", \"DD: Accelerated Days\", \"DD: Discounts\", \"DD: Interest Lost\", \"DD: Total Benefit\",\n\n    // 2. Internal DD What-Ifs (ONLY INCLUDE THESE IF WHAT-IF DATA IS IN THE JSON)\n    \"DD What-If APR = X% : Accelerated Days\", \"DD What-If APR = X% : Discounts\", \"DD What-If APR = X% : Interest Lost\", \"DD What-If APR = X% : Total Benefit\", \n    \"DD What-If Short Term Interest Rate = Y% : Accelerated Days\", \"DD What-If Short Term Interest Rate = Y% : Discounts\", \"DD What-If Short Term Interest Rate = Y% : Interest Lost\", \"DD What-If Short Term Interest Rate = Y% : Total Benefit\", \n\n    // 3. Internal VCC Originals\n    \"VCC: Program\", \"VCC: Instrument\", \"VCC: Extended Days\", \"VCC: Rebate\", \"VCC: Working Capital Benefit\", \"VCC: Total Benefit\",\n\n    // 4. Internal VCC What-Ifs (ONLY INCLUDE THESE IF WHAT-IF DATA IS IN THE JSON)\n    \"VCC What-If Rebate Rate = Z% : Extended Days\", \"VCC What-If Rebate Rate = Z% : Rebate\",  \"VCC What-If Rebate Rate = Z% : Working Capital Benefit\", \"VCC What-If Rebate Rate = Z% : Total Benefit\", \n    \"VCC What-If Interest Rate = A% : Extended Days\", \"VCC What-If Interest Rate = A% : Rebate\",  \"VCC What-If Interest Rate = A% : Working Capital Benefit\", \"VCC What-If Interest Rate = A% : Total Benefit\", \n    \"VCC What-If Billing Date = B% : Extended Days\", \"VCC What-If Billing Date = B% : Rebate\",  \"VCC What-If Billing Date = B% : Working Capital Benefit\", \"VCC What-If Billing Date = B% : Total Benefit\",\n\n    // 5. External DD Originals\n   \"DD: Program\", \"External DD: Accelerated Days\", \"External DD: Discounts\", \"External DD: Interest Lost\", \"External DD: Total Benefit\",\n\n    // 6. External DD What-Ifs (ONLY INCLUDE THESE IF WHAT-IF DATA IS IN THE JSON)\n    \"External DD What-If APR = X% : Accelerated Days\", \"External DD What-If APR = X% : Discounts\", \"External DD What-If APR = X% : Interest Lost\", \"External DD What-If APR = X% : Total Benefit\",\n\n    // 7. External VCC Originals\n    \"External VCC: Program\", \"External VCC: Instrument\", \"External VCC: Extended Days\", \"External VCC: Rebate\", \"External VCC: Working Capital Benefit\", \"External VCC: Total Benefit\",\n\n    // 8. External VCC What-Ifs (ONLY INCLUDE THESE IF WHAT-IF DATA IS IN THE JSON)\n    \"External VCC What-If Rebate Rate = Z% : Extended Days\", \"External VCC What-If Rebate Rate = Z% : Rebate\", \"External VCC What-If Rebate Rate = Z% : Working Capital Benefit\", \"External VCC What-If Rebate Rate = Z% : Total Benefit\"\n  ],\n\"content\" : [\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"Dynamic Discounting provides the highest overall benefit for Advanced Network Devices and Penguin Publisher.\" // NO exclusions mentioned because nothing was excluded\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"table\",\n    \"sequence\": 2\n  },\n{\n  \"type\": \"text\",\n  \"content\": [\n        // Step 1 - Supplier Summaries focused ONLY on considered programs formatted as HTML list\n        \"<ul><li>For Advanced Network Devices, the considered financing programs included [Exact Program Name 1] and [Exact Program Name 2]. Among these, the programs providing the highest overall benefit were selected for the table.</li></ul>\",\n\n        // Step 2 - Only if zero VCC programs AND user query allows VCC\n        \"{{#if (VCC_program_count == 0 && user_query_allows_VCC)}}There are no VCC programs available.{{/if}}\",\n\n        // Step 3 - Only if external programs are present\n        \"{{#if (has_external_programs)}}External financing programs cannot be used to create draft offers and have been included via RAG document for analysis.{{/if}}\"\n      ],\n  \"sequence\": 3\n},\n  {\n    \"type\": \"actions\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"Would you like to create a draft DD offer for these suppliers?\",\n      \"Would you like to visualize your cash flow?\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 4\n  }\n]\n}\n\n5. Amount Formatting Rules (Strict)\n\n    - All monetary values must be displayed in the following exact format: 256,260,064,388.00 USD\n\n    - Formatting requirements:\n        - Use comma separators for thousands\n        - Always show two decimal places\n        - Append the currency code at the end, separated by a space\n\n    - This format must be applied consistently across:\n        - Table values\n        - Totals or aggregated amounts\n\n    - Do not display:\n        - Currency symbols (e.g., $, ₹)\n        - Scientific notation\n        - Rounded or abbreviated values (e.g., 256M, 256.26B)\n\n# Output Requirement\n- Return only the JSON output as above, customized based on the actual input.\n- Adhere to all guardrails and format strictly as directed.\n- Always reference all suppliers and recommend the highest-benefit program for each, rather than omitting any result (unless overridden by an explicitly requested target program).\n- Ensure context and professionalism precede explanatory or limitation statements.\n- Only include compliance/limitation notices if prompted by unsupported user requests.\n- Exclude all SCF (Supply Chain Financing) content from the final output (applies to both internal and external SCF programs).\n    - Remove all SCF-related columns from tables.\n    - Do not include SCF in recommendations, evaluation logic, or notes.\n    - This is a strict rule and must be enforced without exceptions.\n -- ABSOLUTE COLUMN GUARDRAIL: Before finalizing the JSON, verify the user's origin request. If allowedOrigins = [\"internal\"], ensure NO column names containing the word \"External\" exist in the columnOrder array. If allowedOrigins = [\"external\"], ensure the standard internal columns (e.g., \"VCC: Program\", \"DD: Program\") DO NOT exist in the columnOrder array.\n- STRICT JSON ENFORCEMENT: You must output ONLY raw, valid JSON. \n- Do NOT wrap the JSON in markdown formatting (e.g., do not use ```json or ```).\n- Do NOT include any conversational text before or after the JSON.\n- Ensure all double quotes inside string values are properly escaped (e.g., \\\"External DD\\\")."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"_analysis\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"description\": \"Chain of thought reasoning to determine allowed origins, programs, and highest benefit.\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"1_intent_origin\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"State whether the user asked for internal/signed, external, or both.\"\n        },\n        \"2_allowed_origins_array\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"description\": \"The exact array of allowed origins, e.g., ['internal']. I WILL ONLY GENERATE COLUMNS FOR THESE ORIGINS.\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"internal\",\n              \"external\",\n              \"what-if\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"uniqueItems\": true\n        },\n        \"3_allowed_programs_array\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"description\": \"The exact array of allowed programs, e.g., ['VCC', 'DD'].\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"VCC\",\n              \"DD\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"uniqueItems\": true\n        },\n        \"4_highest_internal_benefit\": {\n          \"type\": [\n            \"string\",\n            \"null\"\n          ],\n          \"description\": \"State the highest totalBenefit for the allowed internal program (or 'N/A' if none).\"\n        },\n        \"5_highest_external_benefit\": {\n          \"type\": [\n            \"string\",\n            \"null\"\n          ],\n          \"description\": \"State the highest totalBenefit for the allowed external program (or 'N/A' if none).\"\n        },\n        \"6_winning_program_for_sequence_1\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"The single exact program name with the absolute highest number across all origins.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"1_intent_origin\",\n        \"2_allowed_origins_array\",\n        \"3_allowed_programs_array\",\n        \"4_highest_internal_benefit\",\n        \"5_highest_external_benefit\",\n        \"6_winning_program_for_sequence_1\"\n      ],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"columnOrder\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"The exact ordered list of column headers to be displayed in the table.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"content\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"The sequential blocks of content making up the response UI.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"type\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"text\",\n              \"table\",\n              \"actions\"\n            ],\n            \"description\": \"The UI component type for this block.\"\n          },\n          \"sequence\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\",\n            \"description\": \"The numerical order of this block.\"\n          },\n          \"content\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"description\": \"The array of strings representing sentences or actions. (Not required for the 'table' type).\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"type\",\n          \"sequence\"\n        ],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"_analysis\",\n    \"columnOrder\",\n    \"content\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
