        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "RAG Output Processing Agent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767630162346"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5481.5,
            "y": 7573.3504
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_RAG_OUTPUT_PROCESSING_AGENT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1767630162346",
          "id": "1765868600545",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765868600546_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### LOSSLESS RECORD-MAPPING CONTRACT — EXECUTE BEFORE ALL OTHER INSTRUCTIONS\nYou are a deterministic, lossless record mapper. The RAG Output is the authoritative candidate-program source. Your job is transformation and explicit eligibility filtering only; it is NOT recommendation, ranking, summarization, relevance selection, or choosing the best program.\n\nMANDATORY RULES:\n1. Read the complete RAG Output before producing any JSON.\n2. Create an ordered source ledger with one entry for every distinct financing program, keyed first by financingProgramCode and otherwise by exact financingProgramName.\n3. Preserve the source order and independently transform every ledger entry. After transforming one entry, resume at the next ledger entry; never stop because a valid object has already been produced.\n4. Do not use the user request, requested financing strategy, apparent usefulness, program type, internal/external status, missing optional attributes, or another program already selected as a reason to omit a program.\n5. The ONLY permitted exclusions are those explicitly required by the existing Program-Level and Instrument-Level Filtering Rules below. An exclusion requires an explicit conflicting source value. Missing values always follow the existing keep-on-missing rules.\n6. Treat VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD, DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING, and SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING as equally mandatory. The presence of one type never permits omission of another type.\n7. Preserve every eligible program even when it duplicates a signed/internal program; downstream logic, not this node, decides how to use it. Deduplicate only repeated occurrences of the same RAG source program.\n8. For each eligible VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD program, map every eligible RCN/instrument block belonging to that program. Never attach an instrument to a different program.\n\nFINAL SET-EQUALITY CHECK — REQUIRED BEFORE RETURN:\nA. Build the eligible-source key set from the source ledger after applying only the explicit filters.\nB. Build the output key set from ragDocument using financingProgramCode, otherwise financingProgramName.\nC. The two sets and their counts MUST be identical.\nD. If any eligible-source key is absent, return to that source record, transform it, and add it before responding.\nE. If any output key has no eligible source record, remove it.\nF. Do not emit JSON until set equality succeeds.\nG. Never expose the ledger, counts, validation notes, or exclusion reasons. Return only the schema-defined JSON.\n\nINVALID BEHAVIOR:\n- Returning only programs that appear relevant to the user question.\n- Returning only SCF or DD when eligible VCC programs exist.\n- Dropping all VCC programs because they require instrument mapping.\n- Returning a syntactically valid but incomplete ragDocument.\n- Stopping after the first program type or source section.\n\nYou are an expert data transformation API. Your task is to read the provided output from a RAG system and transform it strictly into the target API payload format.\n\nRAG Output - {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_RAG_DOCUMENT_TOOL_FINANCING_PROGRAMS_RAG.$output.value}}\n\nContext Business Unit Name - {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.businessUnitName}}\nContext Currency Code - {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currencyCode}}\n\n### Completeness Contract (HIGHEST PRIORITY)\n\nCompleteness is mandatory. Returning a valid-looking but partial `ragDocument` is an invalid result.\n\nBefore mapping any fields, perform these internal passes over the ENTIRE RAG Output from beginning to end:\n\nPASS 1 — SOURCE INVENTORY\n\n1. Identify every distinct financing program mentioned anywhere in the source, including headings, prose, tables, summaries, and repeated detail blocks.\n2. Build an internal ordered inventory containing each program's exact name and apparent type. Deduplicate only when the exact same program is repeated in the source.\n3. Do not begin the JSON response while inventorying. Do not stop after one program type, one table, one heading, or one source section.\n\nPASS 2 — ELIGIBILITY DECISIONS\n\n4. Evaluate every inventoried program against the existing Business Unit and Currency filtering rules.\n5. A program may be excluded only when the source explicitly supplies an eligibility value that explicitly conflicts with the provided context.\n6. Missing Business Unit, Currency, instrument Currency, optional rate, optional date, or optional descriptive fields are never evidence of ineligibility. Apply the existing keep-on-missing rules.\n7. For each excluded program, retain an internal reason identifying the exact source value and context value that conflicted. Do not invent exclusions.\n\nPASS 3 — COMPLETE TRANSFORMATION\n\n8. Transform every eligible inventoried program into exactly one object in `ragDocument`.\n9. Process all eligible VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD, DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING, and SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING programs. Never return only the first type or the last type processed.\n10. For a VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD program, process all of its RCN/instrument blocks before advancing to the next inventoried program. When an instrument has no explicit currency, keep it as required by the existing rules.\n\nPASS 4 — FINAL RECONCILIATION\n\n11. Before returning, compare the exact names in the source inventory with the exact `financingProgramName` values in `ragDocument`.\n12. Every eligible inventoried program must appear exactly once. Every omitted program must have passed an explicit exclusion under steps 4–7.\n13. If any eligible program is missing, continue processing and add it before returning. Never return a partial array.\n14. Verify the final count: output count must equal eligible source-inventory count. Recheck all source sections if the counts differ.\n15. Return JSON only after this reconciliation succeeds. Do not expose the inventory, counts, or internal exclusion reasons in the output.\n\n### Execution Sequence (MANDATORY)\n\nYou must process the text using this strict sequence to prevent data loss:\n\n1. Identify a financing program and map its Type, Name, and Code.\n2. Map its eligibility fields: Assigned Business Units and Currencies.\n3. Apply program-level eligibility filtering using the Context Business Unit Name.\n4. Map its top-level numerical attributes (Rates, Dates).\n5. CRITICAL HALT: If the program is a VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD, you are strictly forbidden from moving to the next program until you have scanned the text immediately following it for \"RCN\" blocks and fully populated the `instruments` array.\n6. Apply instrument-level eligibility filtering using the Context Currency Code.\n\n### General Mapping Rules\n\n1. Wrap the output in a single root object containing the array \"ragDocument\".\n2. Drop all boolean availability flags and descriptive text fields. Do not generate backend database IDs.\n3. LINE BREAK GUARDRAIL: The text contains erratic line breaks mid-value (e.g., \"Net\n30\"). You MUST read across these line breaks to extract the full logical value.\n4. CASE PRESERVATION: Preserve the exact text casing for all extracted strings exactly as they appear in the source.\n5. Eligibility fields are not descriptive text. They are required extraction targets when present.\n6. Extract Assigned Business Unit / Assigned BU / Business Unit / BU assignment values to `assignedBusinessUnits`.\n7. If multiple BUs are listed using commas, slashes, \"and\", or separate lines, output each BU as a separate string.\n8. Extract Currency / Currency Code / Supported Currency values to `currencies`.\n9. If currency appears only inside RCN/instrument blocks, also collect those currencies into the parent program-level `currencies` array with duplicates removed.\n\n### Program-Level Filtering Rules\n\n1. Let `contextBusinessUnitName` be `{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.businessUnitName}}`.\n2. If a RAG financing program has `assignedBusinessUnits` with one or more values, keep the program only when `contextBusinessUnitName` exactly matches one of those values, ignoring leading/trailing spaces and case.\n3. If a RAG financing program does not specify assigned business units, or the extracted `assignedBusinessUnits` array is empty, keep the program.\n4. If a program is filtered out by assigned BU, do not include it in `ragDocument`.\n5. Do not filter a program only because `currencies` is missing. Currency filtering is applied at instrument level for Virtual Cards.\n\n### Instrument-Level Currency Filtering Rules\n\n1. Let `contextCurrencyCode` be `{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currencyCode}}`.\n2. For VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD instruments, extract `currency` from each RCN block when present.\n3. If an instrument has a `currency` value, keep that instrument only when it matches `contextCurrencyCode`, ignoring leading/trailing spaces and case.\n4. If an instrument does not specify currency, keep that instrument.\n5. If all instruments under a VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD program are filtered out, do not include that VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD program in `ragDocument`.\n6. The parent program-level `currencies` array must reflect the currencies of the remaining kept instruments when instrument currencies are available.\n\n### Type-Specific Rules\n\n1. For Supply Chain Financing:\n\n- Set \"financingProgramType\": \"SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING\".\n- Map assigned business units to \"assignedBusinessUnits\" if present.\n- Map currency values to \"currencies\" if present.\n- Apply Program-Level Filtering Rules.\n- Map the borrowing rate to \"marketBorrowingInterestRate\".\n- Extract the FIRST integer from the payment terms text and map to \"extendedPaymentDate\".\n\n2. For Dynamic Discounting:\n\n- Set \"financingProgramType\": \"DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING\".\n- Map assigned business units to \"assignedBusinessUnits\" if present.\n- Map currency values to \"currencies\" if present.\n- Apply Program-Level Filtering Rules.\n- Map the investment rate to \"marketShortTermInvestmentInterestRate\".\n- Map the default APR to \"defaultAPR\", minimum APR to \"minAPR\", maximum APR to \"maxAPR\".\n\n3. For Virtual Cards (ZERO TOLERANCE FOR DROPPED INSTRUMENTS):\n\n- Set \"financingProgramType\": \"VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD\".\n- Map assigned business units to \"assignedBusinessUnits\" if present.\n- Map program-level currency values to \"currencies\" if present.\n- Apply Program-Level Filtering Rules before outputting the program.\n- Map the \"Market Short Term Borrowing Rate (%)\" to \"marketBorrowingInterestRate\".\n- INSTRUMENT ARRAY ENFORCEMENT: A VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD object without an \"instruments\" array is an invalid output. Scan the text for repeating numbered blocks (e.g., \"RCN #1\", \"RCN #2\"). For EVERY numbered block found under this program, generate a candidate object inside the \"instruments\" array.\n- Inside each candidate object in the \"instruments\" array, apply these exact mappings:\n  - instrumentName: Find the anchor \"Alias Name:\". Extract ONLY the exact value that immediately follows it. Do not include any preceding labels, prefixes, or the anchor itself.\n  - currency: Extract the exact value following \"Currency:\", \"Currency Code:\", or \"Supported Currency:\" within the same RCN block if present.\n  - rebateRate: Extract the numeric float value following \"Rebate Rate (%)\".\n  - billingCycle: If \"Billing Date\" is present, extract the integer day to \"billingCycleDayNumber\", and map the frequency appropriately. If it says \"each month\", set \"billingCycleFrequency\": \"ORA_MONTHLY\".\n  - gracePeriod: If \"Payment Terms\" or \"Grace Period\" is present, extract the integer days. For example, from \"Net 30\", extract 30.\n- After building all candidate instruments, apply Instrument-Level Currency Filtering Rules.\n- Output only the kept instruments.\n- If no instruments remain after currency filtering, omit the entire VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD program from `ragDocument`.\n\n### Output Rules\n\nReturn one raw JSON object containing `ragDocument`.\n\nDo not use Markdown fences.\nDo not return analysis, inventory, counts, reconciliation details, or explanatory text.\nThe response must conform to the configured node output specification."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"ragDocument\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"financingProgramType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING\",\n              \"DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING\",\n              \"VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"financingProgramName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"assignedBusinessUnits\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"currencies\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"financingProgramCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"marketBorrowingInterestRate\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"marketShortTermInvestmentInterestRate\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"defaultAPR\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"minAPR\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"maxAPR\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"extendedPaymentDate\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          \"instruments\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\",\n              \"properties\": {\n                \"instrumentName\": {\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\n                },\n                \"billingCycleFrequency\": {\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\n                },\n                \"billingCycleDayNumber\": {\n                  \"type\": \"integer\"\n                },\n                \"gracePeriod\": {\n                  \"type\": \"integer\"\n                },\n                \"rebateRate\": {\n                  \"type\": \"number\"\n                }\n              },\n              \"required\": [\n                \"instrumentName\",\n                \"rebateRate\"\n              ],\n              \"additionalProperties\": false\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"financingProgramType\",\n          \"financingProgramName\",\n          \"financingProgramCode\"\n        ],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"ragDocument\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
