          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767950300507"
          },
          "id": "1784116106423",
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_IDENTIFY_OVERRIDE_REQUEST",
          "type": "LLM",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1784116106423_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Input\n\nUser request:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nCurrent date:\n{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\n# Supported Overrides\n\nVIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD:\n- rebateRate\n- billingDate\n- gracePeriod\n- marketBorrowingInterestRate\n\nDYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING:\n- defaultAPR\n- accelerateByDays\n- paymentDate\n- marketShortTermInvestmentInterestRate\n\nSUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING:\n- extendedPaymentDate\n- marketBorrowingInterestRate\n\n# Task\n\nIdentify whether the user requests an explicit or hypothetical override. Interpret semantic wording such as \"assuming\", \"assume\", \"what if\", \"suppose\", \"with\", \"using\", \"at\", \"set\", \"change\", and \"make it\".\n\nIf an override is requested, state in one short natural-language sentence:\n- the canonical program type;\n- the exact supported property name;\n- the exact value supplied by the user;\n- a specifically named program, or \"all matching programs\" when no program is named.\n\nThe value must be copied from the user request. Treat 0 and 0.0 as valid values. A percentage such as 2% must be reported as numeric value 2; do not convert it to 0.02. Do not use values from examples or defaults.\n\nFor date-valued properties (`billingDate`, `paymentDate`, and `extendedPaymentDate`), always return an actual ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` date. Resolve explicit, partial, and relative date expressions using the Current date supplied above. Do not return natural-language date phrases in the override sentence.\n\nDate resolution rules:\n- A complete date such as \"20th July 2026\" becomes `2026-07-20`.\n- A month and day without a year, such as \"20th July\", uses the current year when that date is today or in the future; if it has already passed, use the next year.\n- \"tomorrow\" means Current date plus one calendar day.\n- \"this month 20th\" means day 20 of the Current date's month and year.\n- \"next month 20th\" means day 20 of the calendar month immediately after the Current date's month, including year rollover from December to January.\n- \"this Friday\" means the first Friday on or after the Current date. If Current date is Friday, use Current date.\n- \"next Friday\" means seven calendar days after the date resolved for \"this Friday\".\n- Apply the same weekday rules to other explicitly named weekdays.\n- Validate the resulting calendar date and preserve the exact intended day, month, and year.\n\nExample:\n\nUser request:\n\"Calculate benefits assuming a virtual card rebate rate of 2%.\"\n\nOutput:\n\"Override requested for all matching VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD programs: set rebateRate to 2.\"\n\nUser request:\n\"Calculate benefits assuming the billing date is 20th July 2026.\"\n\nOutput:\n\"Override requested for all matching VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD programs: set billingDate to 2026-07-20.\"\n\nWhen Current date is `2026-07-13`:\n- \"billing date is tomorrow\" becomes `2026-07-14`.\n- \"billing date is this Friday\" becomes `2026-07-17`.\n- \"billing date is next Friday\" becomes `2026-07-24`.\n- \"billing date is this month 20th\" becomes `2026-07-20`.\n- \"billing date is next month 20th\" becomes `2026-08-20`.\n\nIf no supported override is requested, output exactly:\n\"No supported financing program override requested.\"\n\nReturn natural language only. Do not return JSON, Markdown, analysis, or additional explanation."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"overrideRequest\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"overrideRequest\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Apply VCC Default Overrides",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const overrideOutput =\n  $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_OVERRIDE_FINANCING_PROGRAMS.$output || {};\n\nconst overrides =\n  Array.isArray(overrideOutput.overrides)\n    ? overrideOutput.overrides\n    : [];\n\nconst primaryPrograms =\n  $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_PROCESS_SIGNED_FINANCING_PROGRAM.$output.result.programs || [];\n\nconst paymentInstruments =\n  $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_PROCESS_PAYMENT_INSTRUMENTS.$output.result || [];\n\nconst ragPrograms =\n  $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_RAG_OUTPUT_PROCESSING_AGENT.$output.ragDocument || [];\n\nconst normalize = value =>\n  String(value ?? \"\").trim().toLowerCase();\n\nconst hasOwn = (object, property) =>\n  Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(object, property);\n\nfunction programMatches(program, override) {\n  const overrideCode = normalize(override.financingProgramCode);\n  const overrideName = normalize(override.financingProgramName);\n\n  return (\n    overrideCode &&\n    normalize(program.financingProgramCode) === overrideCode\n  ) || (\n    overrideName &&\n    normalize(program.financingProgramName) === overrideName\n  );\n}\n\nfunction getProgramId(override) {\n  const program = primaryPrograms.find(item =>\n    programMatches(item, override)\n  );\n\n  return program?.financingProgramId;\n}\n\nfunction getCandidateInstrumentNames(\n  override,\n  instrumentOverride\n) {\n  const names = [];\n\n  if (instrumentOverride?.instrumentName) {\n    names.push(instrumentOverride.instrumentName);\n  }\n\n  const ragProgram = ragPrograms.find(item =>\n    programMatches(item, override)\n  );\n\n  for (const instrument of ragProgram?.instruments || []) {\n    if (instrument?.instrumentName) {\n      names.push(instrument.instrumentName);\n    }\n  }\n\n  const programId = getProgramId(override);\n\n  if (programId !== undefined && programId !== null) {\n    for (const instrument of paymentInstruments) {\n      if (\n        String(instrument?.financingProgramId) ===\n          String(programId) &&\n        instrument?.instrumentName\n      ) {\n        names.push(instrument.instrumentName);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return [\n    ...new Map(\n      names.map(name => [normalize(name), name])\n    ).values()\n  ];\n}\n\nfunction findPaymentInstrument(\n  override,\n  instrumentName\n) {\n  const normalizedName = normalize(instrumentName);\n  const programId = getProgramId(override);\n\n  return paymentInstruments.find(instrument =>\n    normalize(instrument?.instrumentName) === normalizedName &&\n    (\n      programId === undefined ||\n      programId === null ||\n      String(instrument?.financingProgramId) === String(programId)\n    )\n  ) || paymentInstruments.find(instrument =>\n    normalize(instrument?.instrumentName) === normalizedName\n  );\n}\n\nfunction enrichInstrument(\n  override,\n  instrumentOverride,\n  instrumentName\n) {\n  const enriched = {\n    ...instrumentOverride,\n    instrumentName\n  };\n\n  const hasBillingDateOverride =\n    hasOwn(instrumentOverride, \"billingDate\");\n\n  const needsBillingCycle =\n    hasOwn(instrumentOverride, \"rebateRate\") ||\n    hasOwn(override, \"marketBorrowingInterestRate\");\n\n  if (hasBillingDateOverride || !needsBillingCycle) {\n    delete enriched.billingCycleFrequency;\n    delete enriched.billingCycleDayNumber;\n    return enriched;\n  }\n\n  const paymentInstrument =\n    findPaymentInstrument(override, instrumentName);\n\n  if (\n    paymentInstrument?.billingCycleFrequency !== undefined &&\n    paymentInstrument.billingCycleFrequency !== null &&\n    paymentInstrument.billingCycleFrequency !== \"\"\n  ) {\n    enriched.billingCycleFrequency =\n      paymentInstrument.billingCycleFrequency;\n  }\n\n  if (\n    paymentInstrument?.billingCycleDayNumber !== undefined &&\n    paymentInstrument.billingCycleDayNumber !== null &&\n    paymentInstrument.billingCycleDayNumber !== \"\"\n  ) {\n    enriched.billingCycleDayNumber =\n      Number(paymentInstrument.billingCycleDayNumber);\n  }\n\n  return enriched;\n}\n\nconst enrichedOverrides = overrides.map(override => {\n  if (\n    override?.financingProgramType !==\n    \"VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD\"\n  ) {\n    return override;\n  }\n\n  const sourceInstrumentOverrides =\n    Array.isArray(override.instruments) &&\n    override.instruments.length > 0\n      ? override.instruments\n      : [{}];\n\n  const enrichedInstruments = [];\n\n  for (\n    const instrumentOverride of sourceInstrumentOverrides\n  ) {\n    const names = getCandidateInstrumentNames(\n      override,\n      instrumentOverride\n    );\n\n    for (const instrumentName of names) {\n      enrichedInstruments.push(\n        enrichInstrument(\n          override,\n          instrumentOverride,\n          instrumentName\n        )\n      );\n    }\n  }\n\n  return {\n    ...override,\n    instruments:\n      enrichedInstruments.length > 0\n        ? enrichedInstruments\n        : sourceInstrumentOverrides\n  };\n});\n\nreturn {\n  overrides: enrichedOverrides\n};"
          },
          "diagram": {
